      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In a group of patients with arterial pulmonary hypertension of various origin, the relationship between the relative magnitude of the \"a\" wave of the right apex-cardiogram (ACG) to the total deflection of the ACG (\"a/H ratio\") to both the right atrial \"a\" wave and the right ventricular end-diastolic pressure was studied. Both correlations were statistically significant. The results obtained confirm the ACG value in the non invasive study of the right ventricular function."},
